# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local Docker Compose overrides. Compose auto-loads this file when copied to
# `.env` (which is git-ignored):   cp .env.example .env
#
# Outbound proxy (Netskope corporate proxy at 163.116.128.80:8080).
#
#   • OFF the VPN / direct internet  → leave these BLANK (the default). The api
#     and ollama containers connect directly. This is what makes startup work
#     off-VPN.
#   • ON the corporate VPN           → uncomment the lines below so the api
#     container (Google Maps) and the ollama model pull route through Netskope.
#
# IMPORTANT: this only sets the proxy INSIDE the containers. Docker *image pulls*
# use the daemon's own proxy (configured in WSL, not here). If `docker compose
# up` fails off-VPN with `proxyconnect`, clear the daemon proxy — see README.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# HTTP_PROXY=http://163.116.128.80:8080
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://163.116.128.80:8080
# NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1,api,ollama
